          text Latest  from the Wikimedia technical community. Please tell other users about these changes. Not all changes will affect you.  are available.
          link "tech news" https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Tech/News
          link Translations https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Tech/News/2026/43
          text Updates for editors
          text To measure the impact of incorporating some  on logged-out reader retention, a test for  will be pushed to logged-out readers. With the Image Carousel feature, readers browse community-uploaded images, selected by editors as relevant to specific articles. The test starts on November 20.
          link "community-requested features" https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Readers/Reader_Growth/Image_Browsing#November_2025:_Ideas_and_feedback
          link "Image Carousel" https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Readers/Reader_Growth/Image_Browsing
          text An experimental notice will be pushed to 0.5% of logged-out mobile readers who come to English Wikipedia from Google, asking them to add Wikipedia as a . The test is to see if this notice increases reader retention and encourages people who use Google Search to visit Wikipedia more often. It will run from October 15–29 and will be assessed for its impact on retention and referrals.
          link "Google Preferred Source" https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/preferred-sources/
          text View all 26 community-submitted tasks that were . For example, an issue where  returned an “Access denied” error when users tried to run SQL queries, preventing queries from running normally, has now been fixed.
          image https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Reload_icon_with_two_arrows.svg/20px-Reload_icon_with_two_arrows.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail "Recurrent item"
          link "resolved last week" https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Tech/News/Recently%20resolved%20community%20tasks
          link Quarry https://quarry.wmcloud.org/
          text Updates for technical contributors
          text Due to a long-standing bug, applications that use the  client credentials flow to act on their owners’ behalf are treated as if they are logged out. This will be fixed for new applications registered on or after Monday, October 19. Some affected applications need to re-register.
          image https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Cog-icon-grey.svg/20px-Cog-icon-grey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail "Advanced item"
